      "persona": "Whitehat Hacker",
      "taskMessage": "<b>Mara Voss:</b> Removing one task is insufficient if the account remains overprivileged and new tasks can appear unnoticed. Choose the control set that reduces recurrence and makes change visible.",
      "taskInstructions": "Read <link=\"u04_scheduled_task_persistence\"><u>the NightlyExport persistence condition</u></link>, then select the strongest remediation.",
      "taskQuestion": "Which control set is strongest?",
      "taskCompleteText": "<b>Mara Voss:</b> Correct. Monitor scheduled tasks, rotate service credentials, and apply least privilege to reduce persistence risk.",
      "answers": [
        "Turn off all monitoring completely so that alerts stop interrupting the whole team.",
        "Give every service account the same shared login password.",
        "Leave all of the old scheduled tasks completely undocumented and fully untouched.",
        "Continuously monitor scheduled tasks, rotate all service credentials, and enforce least privilege."
      ],
      "correctAnswer": 3
    },
